rd snow-blind and led by Balmat."}},{"type":"marker","point":[6.85824,45.8784],"label":"Bivouac","style":{"color":"#56b4e9","labelColor":"#56b4e9","haloColor":"#000000","labelPosition":"left","symbol":"base:icon-campsite","labelFont":"noto_sans_bold"},"popup":{"text":"**Gîte à Balmat**\nThe two spent the night of 7 August at the top of the Montagne de la Côte, at the edge of the ice, and started at 4 in the morning."}},{"type":"marker","point":[6.8608,45.87072],"label":"La Jonction","style":{"color":"#56b4e9","labelColor":"#56b4e9","haloColor":"#000000","labelPosition":"right","symbol":"extras:symbol-dot","labelFont":"noto_sans_bold"}},{"type":"marker","point":[6.86144,45.86688],"label":"Grands Mulets","style":{"color":"#56b4e9","labelColor":"#56b4e9","haloColor":"#000000","labelPosition":"left","symbol":"extras:symbol-dot","labelFont":"noto_sans_bold"}},{"type":"marker","point":[6.85888,45.84448],"label":"Grand Plateau","style":{"color":"#56b4e9","labelColor":"#56b4e9","haloColor":"#000000","labelPosition":"left","symbol":"extras:symbol-dot","labelFont":"noto_sans_bold"}},{"type":"marker","point":[6.86528,45.83296],"label":"Mont Blanc, 4,807 m","style":{"color":"#ffffff","labelColor":"#ffffff","haloColor":"#000000","haloWidth":1.5,"size":1.3,"labelSize":1.3,"labelPosition":"top","symbol":"icons:mountain","labelFont":"noto_sans_bold"},"popup":{"text":"**Summit**\nBalmat and Paccard stood on top on 8 August 1786 at 18:23, and stayed for 33 minutes. The climb won the prize that Horace-Bénédict de Saussure had offered in 1760, and is seen as the start of modern mountaineering."}}],"frame":{"bounds":[6.81984,45.69856,6.90688,45.90848],"bearing":-163,"pitch":60},"meta":{"background":{"base":"satellite","streets":false,"labels":"none","colors":{"black":-0.2},"hillshade":true,"terrain":true},"legend":{"entries":[{"type":"line","style":{"color":"#56b4e9","width":4,"arrowEnd":"triangle"},"label":"Balmat and Paccard, 7-8 August 1786"},{"type":"marker","style":{"color":"#56b4e